Existing Method

Step 1 – Initialize Eligibility Flags
  Set isEligible = undefined
  Set primarySkillIsEligible = true
  Set secondarySkillIsEligible = true
  Set otherMandatorySkillIsEligible = true

Step 2 – Extract Required Skill Data
  Get primarySkills from jobRoleData.mandatorySkills.primary
  Get secondarySkills from jobRoleData.mandatorySkills.mandatory
  Get mandatoryCount from jobRoleData.mandatorySkills.mandatoryCount
  Get otherMandatorySkills from jobRoleData.mandatorySkills.otherSkills

Step 3 – Check if there are any skill requirements
  Check: hasNonEmptySkillSet = any item in otherMandatorySkills has non-empty skills list
  IF primarySkills.skills is empty AND secondarySkills is empty AND hasNonEmptySkillSet is false:
    → Set isEligible = true (No skill requirements to validate)

ELSE:
  Step 4 – Validate if candidate has any skills
    IF candidate skills exist:
      → Define helper: computeSkillAndOrIsEligible(skillSet)
         IF skillSet.skills is not empty:
           IF skillSet.type == "AND":
             → Return true only if all skills in skillSet.skills exist in candidate's skills
           ELSE ("OR"):
             → Return true if any skill in skillSet.skills exists in candidate's skills
         ELSE:
           → Return true (nothing to validate)

      Step 5 – Validate Primary Skills
        → Apply computeSkillAndOrIsEligible(primarySkills)
        → Set result to primarySkillIsEligible

      Step 6 – Validate Secondary Skills
        IF secondarySkills exist AND mandatoryCount is defined:
          → Count how many secondarySkills exist in candidate's skills
          → Set secondarySkillIsEligible = true if count >= mandatoryCount

      Step 7 – Validate Other Mandatory Skill Sets
        IF otherMandatorySkills exist:
          → For each skillSet in otherMandatorySkills:
             → Apply computeSkillAndOrIsEligible
          → Set otherMandatorySkillIsEligible = true only if all return true

      Step 8 – Final Eligibility Check
        → Set isEligible = 
              primarySkillIsEligible AND
              secondarySkillIsEligible AND
              otherMandatorySkillIsEligible

    ELSE:
      → Set isEligible = false (no skills provided by candidate)


New Change

Step 1 – Initialize Variables
  Set isEligible = undefined
  Get jobRoleSkills from jobRoleData.jobRoleSkills
  Initialize empty list: mandatorySkillIds = []

Step 2 – Extract Mandatory Skill IDs
  IF jobRoleSkills exists:
    FOR each skill in jobRoleSkills:
      IF skill.isMandatory is true:
        → Add skill.skillId to mandatorySkillIds list

Step 3 – Check Eligibility Based on Mandatory Skills
  IF mandatorySkillIds is empty:
    → Set isEligible = true (no mandatory skills to validate)

  ELSE:
    → Set isEligible = true only if every ID in mandatorySkillIds is present in candidate’s skills array
    (i.e., candidate must have all mandatory skills)

    → If even one mandatory skill is missing, set isEligible = false
